1
00:00:05,992 --> 00:00:17,402
They murdered my past, they tore her away,
With cold-blooded rules and the things they would say.

2
00:00:17,566 --> 00:00:29,964
So I built up a wall, kept my new love unseen,
To protect my sweet Luna from where they had been.

3
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:42,223
Now the secret is out, and the armor is gone,
My worst kind of nightmare is starting to dawn!

4
00:00:43,238 --> 00:00:55,163
If they know her name, they will tear us apart,
Their rules and their silence will poison her heart!

5
00:00:55,635 --> 00:01:06,822
I kept her a whisper, a glow in the dark,
With no parental eyes to extinguish our spark.

6
00:01:07,169 --> 00:01:19,747
She was mine, she was safe, in a world of my own,
A beautiful sanctuary they shouldn't be shown.

7
00:01:20,179 --> 00:01:32,207
The conductor walked in, brought his flowers and cheer,
But with one clumsy word, he unleashed my deep fear.

8
00:01:32,598 --> 00:01:44,806
“How did Luna react?”—and the room turned to stone,
My sanctuary broken, my hiding place blown.

9
00:01:45,211 --> 00:01:56,596
My mother kneels down, speaks of holding her tight,
She smiles in my face and she softens the fright.

10
00:01:56,929 --> 00:02:09,618
But the shadows are waiting, the trap has been set,
This brief, golden moment is as good as it gets.

11
00:02:10,134 --> 00:02:21,466
I wanted to save her, I tried to run free,
But the ghost of their rules was still hunting me.

12
00:02:22,622 --> 00:02:34,985
The phone is now silent, the echoes remain,
Will they love her as I do, or leave me in pain?

